pe": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you write an e-mail.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.</br> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ied</span>.</br>  Irregular verbs change in different ways.</br> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"italic\">did</span> followed by the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask ... ?</span></br>  <span class=\"italic\">Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"italic\">to do</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to decide\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"decided\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to copy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"copied\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to protect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"protected\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to lose\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"lost\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to say\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"said\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to speak\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spoke\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thought\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Present vs. Present Continuous Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Present tense to talk about:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul> <li>a routine action or specific action that happens regularly</li> <li>a general truth</li> <li>to give personal information</li> </ul> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use expressions of frequency like every day or always with the Present Simple.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You form the Present Continuous with the verb <span class=\"strong\">to be + verb-ing</span>.</br></br>  You use the Present Continuous tense to talk about:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul> <li>a current event or action happening around now</li> <li>events that <span class=\"strong\">are going to happen</span> soon (future plans)</li> </ul> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use expressions like <span class=\"italic\">right now</span> or <span class=\"italic\">later</span> with the Present Continuous.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I know it's hard for you to get there without a car.</br></br> Don't worry about meeting me at the airport. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm writing to tell you that I'm coming to San Francisco.</br></br>  I'm arriving on December 15th.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dear", "type": "name"}, {"content": "A salutation you use at the beginning of a letter or e-mail", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Dear Vanessa, ... ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "vacation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "time away from work", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I decided that it's just too long to wait until summer vacation to see you! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take time off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stop working for a period of time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I told my boss that I'm taking two weeks off and she said that it was OK with her. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Christmas", "type": "name"}, {"content": "traditional celebration on December 25th", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm arriving on December 15th, so we'll get ready for Christmas together!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "spoke", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the verb <span class=\"italic\">to speak</span> in the Simple Past tense", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I spoke to my cousin, Wendy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pick up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get someone from a certain place, usually in a car", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She's picking me up from the airport when I arrive.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "flight details", "type": "name"}, {"content": "information about an airplane flight, such as time of departure and arrival", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'll send you the flight details when I get them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "car", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a motorized vehicle", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I know it's hard for you to get there without a car. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le04ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose 7 different countries.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go online. Find out how many vacation days people in each country are entitled to each year.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down countries and the days in order from highest to lowest. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss your findings with a partner. Which country has the best system?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research vacation days in 7 countries.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write the list in order from highest to lowest.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss the list of countries and vacation days with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}]}